    <bpmn:process id="W_W3381" name="W3381. Extended-Terms / Payable-Restructuring Negotiation &amp; Vendor Agreement" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Working-capital initiative; vendor contract renewal; strategic vendor review
Frequency: Periodic
Volume: Top ~100–200 vendors; ~20–40 term changes/year
Owner: Procurement Director
Participants: Procurement, Treasury Manager, Category Managers (links to VS-01), Vendor (links to VS-03.3)
Source: workflow W3381 — Extended-Terms / Payable-Restructuring Negotiation &amp; Vendor Agreement</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3381_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3381_Lane1" name="Treasury Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3381_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3381_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3381_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W3381_Lane2" name="Category Managers">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3381_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3381_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3381_Start4" name="Working-capital initiative; vendor contract renewal; strategic vendor review">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3381_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3381_Task5" name="Treasury/Procurement identify term-extension candidates from working-capital…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Treasury/Procurement identify term-extension candidates from working-capital analytics (links to W3393): high-spend, stable, low-risk vendors where extended terms (e.g., Net 30→60) plus SCF access improves BuildRight DPO without harming the vendor
Responsible (R): Treasury Manager / Procurement
Accountable (A): Procurement Director
Duration: Quarterly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3381_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3381_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3381_Task6" name="Category Managers/Procurement negotiate extended terms with the vendor, bundled…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Category Managers/Procurement negotiate extended terms with the vendor, bundled with SCF enrollment (W3379) and/or volume commitment (links to VS-39 rebates); price-for-terms analysis ensures the term gain is not offset by a price increase; update the contract (links to VS-03.3) and payment-terms master (links to W295)
Responsible (R): Category Managers / Procurement
Accountable (A): Procurement Director
Duration: Per vendor</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3381_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3381_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3381_Task7" name="Treasury/AP update system payment terms, communicate to AP (links to VS-15) and…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Treasury/AP update system payment terms, communicate to AP (links to VS-15) and the SCF platform, and re-baseline the cash forecast (links to VS-18.1) and DPO target (W3393); monitor vendor behavior for adverse reaction
Responsible (R): Treasury Manager / AP Manager
Accountable (A): Treasury Manager
Duration: Per change</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3381_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3381_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3381_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3381_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-544 (ensure controlled execution — Supplier Finance &amp; Reverse-Factoring Program Management (PA-105.1).) | - operational: price-for-terms analytics; operational: SCF access (W3379) and vendor-health screening
Owner: Procurement Director</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
