    <bpmn:process id="W_W3384" name="W3384. SCF Program Risk, Concentration &amp; Counterparty Governance" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Monthly/quarterly program governance review
Frequency: Monthly + quarterly
Volume: Full SCF program
Owner: CFO
Participants: CFO, Treasury Manager, Procurement Director, Risk (links to VS-21.2), Internal Audit (links to VS-21)
Source: workflow W3384 — SCF Program Risk, Concentration &amp; Counterparty Governance</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3384_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3384_Lane1" name="Treasury Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3384_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3384_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3384_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W3384_Lane2" name="CFO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3384_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3384_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3384_Start4" name="Monthly/quarterly program governance review">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3384_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3384_Task5" name="Treasury/Risk compile the SCF program risk view: funder concentration, vendor…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Treasury/Risk compile the SCF program risk view: funder concentration, vendor concentration (top-10 funded), segment exposure (import/local), recourse/true-sale status, covenant headroom (W3382), and vendor-credit/delinquency trends (links to VS-68 methodology)
Responsible (R): Treasury Manager / Risk
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: Monthly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3384_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3384_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3384_Task6" name="Treasury/Procurement review program performance vs targets (DPO gain…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Treasury/Procurement review program performance vs targets (DPO gain, finance-cost yield, vendor adoption, exception rate), assess vendor-health signals and macro/import risk (links to VS-02.3/VS-87), and decide program adjustments (pricing, eligibility, limit)
Responsible (R): Treasury Manager / Procurement
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: Quarterly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3384_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3384_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3384_Task7" name="CFO report SCF program status, risk, and working-capital outcome to executive…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: CFO report SCF program status, risk, and working-capital outcome to executive committee (links to VS-33.2) and Internal Audit (links to VS-21); ensure SOX-equivalent controls, segregation of duties, and audit-trail integrity
Responsible (R): CFO / Treasury Manager
Accountable (A): CEO / Board
Duration: Quarterly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3384_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3384_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3384_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3384_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-106 (ensure SCF settlement &amp; covenant compliance.) | - operational: multi-funder design and concentration limits; operational: internal-audit review (links to VS-21) and continuous control monitoring
Owner: CFO</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W3384_Assoc10" sourceRef="W3384_Annotation9" targetRef="W3384_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
